<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.32.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.32.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.32.0 (2026-11-24): The chapter 11 concept panel story is done. All 42 Try it runs of the 64 concept panels are the book's lines (or named programs) with a hidden set-up; page 9.23.0 passes the full page test."""@en .

ex:TK11_Concepts_11_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "New files: A-box 03-materials/ch11/rdodi/sen0414_ch11_domain_abox_v1_0_2.ttl (made by 08-tooling/try_it_abox_make_v1_0_0.py from 08-tooling/ch11-page/try_it_ch11_v1_0_0.json: the I/O example of each of 42 concepts replaced), set-ups 08-tooling/ch11-page/try_it_setup_v1_0_0.json, page 03-materials/ch11/page/sen0414_ch11_page_v9_23_0.html, with the tools of register 1.30.0. Each code is a line or block of the book chapter read from the book file or a named program; paths are relative to the page's own working folder; sorted() or in-place sorts fix the order where the book's order depends on the computer (dry run, walk, glob); the error of a missing folder is caught and named because its number differs between computers. Page 9.22.0 and A-box 1.0.1 stay unchanged." .
ex:TK11_Concepts_11_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/ch11-page/logs_v9_23_0: code check C1 to C5 0 findings (19 examples); full page test 9.40.0: exit 0, 410 features passed, 0 failed, widgets 64 of 64. A direct run of all 42 Try it examples in the browser found the missing-folder error text differing (error number 44 against 2) before the test; the example was changed to name the error type. Open: outputs are recorded under Linux (PosixPath where the book shows WindowsPath)." .
ex:ST11_Concepts_11 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met for chapter 11: every Try it run of the concept panels is the book's code with its hidden set-up, runs in the browser and the page test passes." .
